{
  "course": "初中60短文",
  "passage": 58,
  "title": "Passage 58",
  "voice": "温暖自然英式女老师｜IndexTTS2.5 慢速教学",
  "sentences": [
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 1,
      "sourceSentenceId": 1,
      "chunkId": "s58-p01",
      "image": "assets/images/01.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p01.mp3",
      "en": "Wukong, Tiangong, Tianwen ... Do you know where the names of Chinese space programmes come from?",
      "cn": "悟空、天宫、天问……你知道这些中国航天项目名称的由来吗？"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 2,
      "sourceSentenceId": 2,
      "chunkId": "s58-p02",
      "image": "assets/images/02.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p02.mp3",
      "en": "The well-known moon mission Chang'e is named after a goddess who flew to the moon.",
      "cn": "著名的登月任务“嫦娥”就是以一位飞向月亮的仙女的名字命名的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 3,
      "sourceSentenceId": 3,
      "chunkId": "s58-p03",
      "image": "assets/images/03.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p03.mp3",
      "en": "This mission was important in studying the moon's surface.",
      "cn": "这项任务在对月球表面的研究方面十分重要。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 4,
      "sourceSentenceId": 4,
      "chunkId": "s58-p04",
      "image": "assets/images/04.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p04.mp3",
      "en": "Wukong, the dark matter particle explorer, is named after a Chinese superhero, Monkey King.",
      "cn": "“悟空”，即暗物质粒子探测卫星，是以中国的超级英雄美猴王的名字命名的。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 5,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s58-p05-01",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p05-01.mp3",
      "en": "According to Journey to the West,",
      "cn": "根据《西游记》，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 6,
      "sourceSentenceId": 5,
      "chunkId": "s58-p05-02",
      "image": "assets/images/05.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p05-02.mp3",
      "en": "Monkey King has a pair of sharp eyes which can tell the difference between good and evil.",
      "cn": "美猴王（孙悟空）有一双敏锐的眼睛，能够分辨善恶。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 7,
      "sourceSentenceId": 6,
      "chunkId": "s58-p06",
      "image": "assets/images/06.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p06.mp3",
      "en": "The Wukong satellite is just as sharp-eyed as Monkey King to help scientists search for dark matter in space.",
      "cn": "悟空号卫星就如同美猴王一样目光敏锐，能够帮助科学家在太空中寻找暗物质。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 8,
      "sourceSentenceId": 7,
      "chunkId": "s58-p07",
      "image": "assets/images/07.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p07.mp3",
      "en": "The name of the space station, Tiangong, means 'Heavenly Palace'.",
      "cn": "空间站的名字“天宫”意为“天上的宫殿”。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 9,
      "sourceSentenceId": 8,
      "chunkId": "s58-p08",
      "image": "assets/images/08.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p08.mp3",
      "en": "In Chinese myths, this is the home of Tian Di.",
      "cn": "在中国神话中，这是天帝的家。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 10,
      "sourceSentenceId": 9,
      "chunkId": "s58-p09",
      "image": "assets/images/09.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p09.mp3",
      "en": "Now, Tiangong Space Station is a home for Chinese astronauts in space.",
      "cn": "现在，天宫空间站是中国航天员在太空中的家。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 11,
      "sourceSentenceId": 10,
      "chunkId": "s58-p10",
      "image": "assets/images/10.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p10.mp3",
      "en": "Tianwen, China's Mars mission, gets its name from the poem Tianwen by Qu Yuan.",
      "cn": "中国的火星任务“天问”取名于屈原的诗《天问》。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 12,
      "sourceSentenceId": 11,
      "chunkId": "s58-p11",
      "image": "assets/images/11.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p11.mp3",
      "en": "Qu Yuan is a well-known poet from ancient China.",
      "cn": "屈原是中国古代著名的诗人。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 13,
      "sourceSentenceId": 12,
      "chunkId": "s58-p12",
      "image": "assets/images/12.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p12.mp3",
      "en": "In Tianwen, he had questions about the sky, stars, nature, myths and the real world, showing his hunger for truth.",
      "cn": "在《天问》中，他对天空、星辰、自然、神话和现实世界提出了疑问，展现了他对真理的渴求。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 14,
      "sourceSentenceId": 13,
      "chunkId": "s58-p13",
      "image": "assets/images/13.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p13.mp3",
      "en": "Perhaps the Tianwen missions will end up answering some of Qu Yuan's questions.",
      "cn": "也许“天问”任务最终能够回答屈原的一些问题。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 15,
      "sourceSentenceId": 14,
      "chunkId": "s58-p14",
      "image": "assets/images/14.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p14.mp3",
      "en": "If you look into more names of Chinese space programmes, you will find that they all have beautiful meanings.",
      "cn": "如果你深入探究更多中国航天项目的名字，就会发现它们都蕴含着美好的寓意。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 16,
      "sourceSentenceId": 15,
      "chunkId": "s58-p15",
      "image": "assets/images/15.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p15.mp3",
      "en": "We, the Chinese people, have a long-cherished space dream.",
      "cn": "我们中国人民怀揣着悠久的航天梦想。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 17,
      "sourceSentenceId": 16,
      "chunkId": "s58-p16",
      "image": "assets/images/16.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p16.mp3",
      "en": "Therefore, the naming of Chinese space programmes is taken very seriously.",
      "cn": "因此，我们对中国的航天项目命名十分认真。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 18,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s58-p17-01",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p17-01.mp3",
      "en": "Scientists, from junior members to experienced leaders,",
      "cn": "科学家们，从基层成员到经验丰富的领导者，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 19,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s58-p17-02",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p17-02.mp3",
      "en": "are also working hard to sweep away setbacks,",
      "cn": "也都在努力工作，克服障碍，"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 20,
      "sourceSentenceId": 17,
      "chunkId": "s58-p17-03",
      "image": "assets/images/17.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p17-03.mp3",
      "en": "without letting any challenges disappoint them.",
      "cn": "不让任何挑战使他们灰心。"
    },
    {
      "cover": false,
      "sentenceId": 21,
      "sourceSentenceId": 18,
      "chunkId": "s58-p18",
      "image": "assets/images/18.png",
      "audio": "assets/audio/segments/s58-p18.mp3",
      "en": "The names are like postcards to the world, showing our determination in space exploration.",
      "cn": "这些名字就像寄往世界的明信片，展示了我们探索太空的决心。"
    }
  ],
